      "notes": "Public attachments contract (max 5 files, 2 MiB/file, 5 MiB total decoded), bounded-decode acceptance pipeline with structural file-type validation (PDF/JPEG/PNG/DOCX/XLSX/CSV/TXT), durable short-lived spool with startup+periodic reconciliation, request-unique provider submission evidence (at-most-once invocation, explicit ADR 0015 attempt_number exception), DeliveryUnknown terminal state, attachment manual-retry/cancel prohibition, shared SQLite backup maintenance lease, ACS/SMTP provider mapping with forced Base64 CTE, and Admin filename masking with an audited reveal action. Native AOT publish smoke could not run on this Windows dev host (cross-OS AOT compilation is unsupported); CI (ubuntu) performs it on the PR. Crash-window fault-injection and 256/512 MiB Docker/cgroup resource qualification were not performed in this environment.",
